{"key":"enterprise/T1574.006","id":"T1574.006","name":"Dynamic Linker Hijacking","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1574","tactics":["execution","stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may execute their own malicious payloads by hijacking environment variables the dynamic linker uses to load shared libraries. During the execution preparation phase of a program, the dynamic linker loads specified absolute paths of shared libraries from various environment variables and files, such as LD_PRELOAD on Linux or DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES on macOS. Libraries specified in environment variables are loaded first, taking…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1574/006","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--633a100c-b2c9-41bf-9be5-905c1b16c825","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.636Z","source_object_version":"3.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0034","name":"Process Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0034","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--ee575f4a-2d4f-48f6-b18b-89067760adc1","page":"telemetry/DC0034/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0435","name":"Detection Strategy for Hijack Execution Flow: Dynamic Linker Hijacking","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0435","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--da2107bd-4733-4d0b-a35c-33f7883e9ae9","relationship_id":"relationship--7cc0a19d-6627-483b-9de1-a723124fa736"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1209","name":"Analytic 1209","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0435#AN1209","guidance":"Detection focuses on identifying abuse of LD_PRELOAD and related linker variables. Defender perspective: monitor unexpected setting or modification of LD_PRELOAD in shell initialization scripts or environment exports, file creation of suspicious shared libraries, and correlation of these modifications with anomalous process execution. Key signals include execve events with LD_PRELOAD defined, newly created .so files in user directories, and processes hooking libc functions exhibiting abnormal behavior.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0435"},{"id":"AN1210","name":"Analytic 1210","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0435#AN1210","guidance":"Detection centers on DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES and DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH abuse. Defender perspective: monitor for modification of these environment variables in shell or plist files, file creation of dylibs in user-controlled paths, and correlation of environment variable usage with unexpected module loads by user applications. Suspicious indicators include processes with DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES set, execution of applications loading untrusted dylibs, and anomalies in module load history.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0435"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"execve with LD_PRELOAD or linker-related environment variables set","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1209","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0435#AN1209","validation":"upstream_definition_not_l